    "comment": "Distance: 1500 Meters Conditions: Float starts on the Connecticut River.  Current was almost non existent, due to the current going out while the tide came in.  Ten mph tail wind with moderate chop & occasional 20 mph gusts. Race course requires a slight turn to port at approximately the 750 meter mark. Comments: MHS Boys 1V 3 seat jumped a slide approximately 1200 meters into the race & had to stop rowing until the athlete returned to their seat.\r\n\r\nValley Regional Boys 2V incurred a 10 second penalty for cutting the turn to port too early, shortening the course by going on the wrong side of the buoy. Original time was 5:38.95.\r\n\r\nGirls 2V Race included Middletown B Boat (Their 3V boat in a 2V race) that came in 2nd.\r\n\r\nNote for CPSRA: 4th boats are novice races.  We also did a mixed novice 8. Times below:\r\n\r\nEO Smith: 6:22.34\r\nMHS 6:43.53  - 4 seat caught two craps causing all rowers to stop both times.\r\n\nNone",
